  partName: Exhaust Manifold Bolt (2)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold Bolt (2) is a tiny, elongated bolt located at
    the bottom-center-front of the engine, playing a crucial role in securing the
    exhaust manifold in place. Its primary function is to withstand high temperatures
    and pressures, ensuring a tight seal and preventing exhaust gas leaks. Interestingly,
    the bolt's material, Material.001, is designed to resist corrosion and wear,
    even in harsh engine environments.
